                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e4eb41ce-6280-375b-b2a3-df706e12f0dd",
                        "entry_id": "82cba0f3-6fef-3897-8835-dc1c1416942a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Someone who dies by drowning."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c3088c9e-6102-4135-9a63-016c6656f26e",
                                "sense_id": "e4eb41ce-6280-375b-b2a3-df706e12f0dd",
                                "text": "With the jumpers and the drowners, McGee, you don't pick up a pattern. That's because a jumper damned near always makes it the first time, and a drowner is usually almost as successful, about the same rate as hangers."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "4de6b2a9-f57e-3b0c-a91b-a80057ac4edd",
                        "entry_id": "82cba0f3-6fef-3897-8835-dc1c1416942a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "One who drowns another."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "9e990699-c4d7-4c95-9b81-c97fc4cefd6c",
                                "sense_id": "4de6b2a9-f57e-3b0c-a91b-a80057ac4edd",
                                "text": "At eight you thought of boys as cat drowners and bird stoners. At nine there was another reason for boys' existence: they either noticed you or they didn't, and it desperately mattered which."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "fd388217-41f8-4252-9f09-b8d97f546ab9",
                        "source_entry_id": "82cba0f3-6fef-3897-8835-dc1c1416942a",
                        "source_sense_description": "someone who dies by drowning",
                        "target_lang_word": "noyé",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "noyé",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6a844d14-b3f0-3484-99f8-d05b4237f3fc",
                                        "entry_id": "189a8652-bc32-3f5b-b339-df8b5026457a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Personne qui se noie ou qui a péri par noyade."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Mort"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8a3fb01b-cfe3-485f-9d99-9a08513cf980",
                                                "sense_id": "6a844d14-b3f0-3484-99f8-d05b4237f3fc",
                                                "text": "Un grondement immense enveloppait la côte.\nSur les flots palpitaient, blêmes, de toutes parts,\nLes âmes des noyés qui moururent en faute."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e89027cc-e829-4730-a2eb-548532c93b3a",
                                                "sense_id": "6a844d14-b3f0-3484-99f8-d05b4237f3fc",
                                                "text": "Des hoquets de dégoût convulsèrent de nouveau leurs faces hâlées, zébrées de rides : depuis un mois, ils avaient bu de l’eau dans laquelle mijotait ce noyé ; depuis un mois tout le pays s’abreuvait de cette pourriture."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "noyé",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c755713b-4f7b-3ae8-97fb-cda10a5eecd8",
                                        "entry_id": "253c2c24-b275-34bf-b607-32f2301fe7df",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Mort par noyade."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Mort"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "91ea26cb-b068-4f9e-881a-356b241a3261",
                                                "sense_id": "c755713b-4f7b-3ae8-97fb-cda10a5eecd8",
                                                "text": "Elle était hantée par l’image obsédante d’un enfant noyé."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "936125b3-4d75-3e9d-882e-7f859cb86ac9",
                                        "entry_id": "253c2c24-b275-34bf-b607-32f2301fe7df",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Inondé, recouvert par l’eau."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b59a9189-c22f-4dd3-9817-71215a651338",
                                                "sense_id": "936125b3-4d75-3e9d-882e-7f859cb86ac9",
                                                "text": "Depuis l’inondation, les pages de son carnet avaient disparu, noyées sous les eaux."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f4ed27f4-87c3-38d3-b8a7-2ea173e58ae9",
                                        "entry_id": "253c2c24-b275-34bf-b607-32f2301fe7df",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Perdu, égaré, dépassé."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bf09782d-ac6e-4e85-a469-688defa3661a",
                                                "sense_id": "f4ed27f4-87c3-38d3-b8a7-2ea173e58ae9",
                                                "text": "Mais ni mes regrets, ni ma compassion ne justifiaient l’ouragan qui me dévasta pendant deux jours : je ne supportais pas ce regard noyé que mon oncle avait jeté à sa femme, juste avant de mourir, et où déjà l’irréparable était accompli."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
